---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import { CONTACT } from '../../data/site';

const breadcrumbs = [{ name: 'Our prices', url: '/funeral-costs/' }];
---

<Page
  title="Funeral Costs in Dunbar & East Lothian"
  heading="What a funeral costs"
  description="Our funeral prices, published in full: Standardised Price List, Additional Options Price List, and help available with funeral costs in Scotland."
  standfirst="You should never have to ask twice what something costs, or find out at the end."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <p>
    Money is the thing families are most reluctant to raise and most anxious about. So we
    publish everything, we say it out loud before you ask, and we give you a written
    estimate before you commit to anything at all.
  </p>

  <h2>The three lists</h2>

  <h3><a href="/funeral-costs/standardised-price-list/">Standardised Price List</a></h3>
  <p>
    The headline prices for an attended and an unattended funeral, in the format every UK
    funeral director is required to use. This is the one to compare against other funeral
    directors, because the format is fixed and the same things are included.
  </p>

  <h3>
    <a href="/funeral-costs/additional-options-price-list/">Additional Options Price List</a>
  </h3>
  <p>
    Everything else you might choose — coffins, cars, flowers, notices, memorials —
    itemised. All of it optional.
  </p>

  <h3>
    <a href="/funeral-costs/help-with-funeral-costs/">Help with funeral costs</a>
  </h3>
  <p>
    Funeral Support Payment and other help available in Scotland. We will help you apply,
    and once you have, it can be paid directly to us so the money never has to pass
    through your hands.
  </p>

  <Callout title="One thing to watch when you compare">
    <p>
      Always ask whether a quoted price <em>includes the crematorium or burial fee</em>.
      Some advertised prices are the funeral director's own charges only, with several
      hundred pounds of third-party fees added afterwards. Our lists make plain which is
      which, and you are entitled to that clarity from anyone you ask.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>What drives the cost</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Burial or cremation.</strong> Burial usually costs more, mainly because of
      the lair purchase and interment fee, both of which are council charges rather than
      ours.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Whether anyone attends.</strong> A{' '}
      <a href="/funeral-services/direct-cremation/">direct cremation</a> costs
      considerably less than an attended funeral.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The coffin.</strong> The range is wide. Recycled cardboard is the least
      expensive, solid hardwood the most, with the woven eco coffins in between.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cars, flowers and printing.</strong> All optional, and easily the part
      families most often decide they do not need.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Paying</h2>
  <p>
    Our invoice is normally due within 30 days of the funeral. Where the estate is
    settling it, we will invoice the estate and wait — banks will usually release funds
    for a funeral bill before anything else is resolved. If you need longer, ask. We
    would rather agree something workable than have a family avoid the telephone.
  </p>

  <Callout tone="accent">
    <p>
      To ask what anything costs, telephone{' '}
      <a href={CONTACT.phoneHref} class="font-semibold">{CONTACT.phone}</a>. Nobody will
      try to sell you anything.
    </p>
  </Callout>
</Page>
